  'Option D (correct) is HTTP APIs. Amazon API Gateway HTTP APIs are designed for building low-latency, cost-effective, and simpler APIs that are ideal for integrating with AWS Lambda functions or HTTP backends. Option A (WebSocket APIs) are for real-time, two-way communication. Option B (REST APIs) offer more features like request/response transformation, caching, and custom authorizers, but are generally more expensive and have higher latency than HTTP APIs. Option C (Private APIs) are for exposing APIs only within a VPC.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_1_43',
  'A developer is creating an AWS Lambda function that performs a short, bursty task, typically completing within a few seconds. To avoid unnecessary costs and resource consumption, what is the most appropriate timeout configuration for this function?',
  'mcq',
  '["Set the timeout to the maximum allowed (15 minutes) to prevent any premature termination.","Configure the timeout to be slightly longer than the expected maximum execution time.","Use the default timeout setting provided by AWS Lambda.","Set the timeout to 1 second to ensure immediate termination if it hangs."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the best practice for setting Lambda timeouts. Configuring the timeout to be slightly longer than the expected maximum execution time allows the function to complete its task while preventing it from running indefinitely and incurring unnecessary costs or consuming concurrency if it hangs. Option A (Setting the timeout to the maximum allowed) is an anti-pattern because it allows hung functions to consume concurrency budget and incur unnecessary cost. Option C (Using the default timeout) might be too long for short tasks, leading to wasted resources. Option D (Setting the timeout to 1 second) is likely too short and would cause legitimate invocations to fail prematurely.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_1',
  'easy'
);

