  'Option D (correct) is Amazon EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service). EKS is a fully managed service that allows you to run Kubernetes on AWS without needing to manage the Kubernetes control plane. Option A (Amazon EC2) provides virtual servers, which can host Kubernetes but require manual management. Option B (Amazon ECS) is a container orchestration service that uses its own scheduler, not Kubernetes. Option C (AWS App Runner) is a fully managed service for deploying containerized web applications and APIs, but it''s not a Kubernetes service.',
