  '{0}',
  'Option A (correct) is AWS Security Token Service (STS), specifically the AssumeRole API operation, which allows you to obtain temporary security credentials that you can use to access AWS resources. This is crucial for cross-account access and federated identities. Option B, AWS IAM, is used for managing permanent users and roles. Option C, AWS KMS, is for encryption key management. Option D, AWS Secrets Manager, is for managing application secrets.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
