  'Option A (correct) is Amazon Cognito User Pools, which provides a scalable user directory that handles user sign-up, sign-in, and profile management for web and mobile applications. Option B, Amazon Cognito Identity Pools, is used to authorize users to access AWS services after they have been authenticated. Option C, AWS IAM, is for managing access to AWS resources, not for application-level user directories. Option D, AWS Organizations, is for managing AWS accounts.',
