  '{2}',
  'Option C (Amazon Cognito Identity Pools) is the correct service. Identity Pools are used to vend temporary AWS credentials to users who have authenticated through a User Pool or other identity providers (like Facebook, Google, or SAML). These temporary credentials grant access to specific AWS resources. Option A (Amazon Cognito User Pools) handles user sign-up, sign-in, and directory management, providing JWT tokens for application-level authentication, but not direct AWS credentials. Option B (AWS Identity and Access Management) manages permanent users, roles, and permissions within an AWS account, but doesn''t directly handle federated user credential vending for applications. Option D (AWS Security Token Service) is the underlying service that Cognito Identity Pools use to vend temporary credentials, but Identity Pools provide the direct integration and management layer for this specific use case.',
