  '["AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) for user credentials.","AWS Key Management Service (KMS) for encryption keys.","AWS Secrets Manager for storing and retrieving application secrets.","Amazon CloudWatch for monitoring and logging."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is AWS Secrets Manager. It provides a dedicated API for applications to retrieve secrets, such as database credentials, at runtime. This prevents hardcoding secrets and allows for centralized management and rotation. Option A, AWS IAM, manages access to AWS services, not application secrets directly. Option B, AWS KMS, manages encryption keys. Option D, Amazon CloudWatch, is for monitoring and logging.',
