  'Which AWS service offers built-in automatic rotation for database credentials and API keys, enhancing security by regularly changing sensitive values?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (SecureString), for encrypted parameters.","AWS Key Management Service (KMS), for managing encryption keys.","Amazon S3, for storing encrypted objects.","AWS Secrets Manager, for automatic secret rotation."]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (correct) is AWS Secrets Manager. It is specifically designed to provide automatic rotation for various types of secrets, including database credentials and API keys, which significantly improves security posture. Option A, AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (SecureString), can store encrypted secrets but does not support automatic rotation. Option B, AWS KMS, manages encryption keys but does not rotate the secrets themselves. Option C, Amazon S3, is object storage and not a secret management service with rotation capabilities.',
