  'Option A (Use AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) templates to define and deploy the serverless resources) is the most efficient and recommended approach. AWS SAM simplifies the definition and deployment of serverless applications, ensuring consistency across environments. Option B (Manually create each Lambda function and API Gateway endpoint in the AWS Management Console for each environment) is prone to errors and lacks consistency. Option C (Write custom scripts to call the AWS CLI for each resource creation and update) is better than manual creation but less declarative and maintainable than SAM. Option D (Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to deploy the serverless application) is designed for traditional web applications, not specifically for serverless architectures like Lambda and API Gateway.',
