  'Option C (AWS SAM) is the correct choice. AWS SAM is an open-source framework that extends AWS CloudFormation to provide a simplified way of defining, previewing, and deploying serverless applications. It allows developers to define Lambda functions, API Gateway APIs, DynamoDB tables, and other serverless resources in a concise YAML or JSON template. Option A (AWS CloudFormation) is a general-purpose infrastructure as code service, but SAM provides serverless-specific abstractions that simplify template writing. Option B (AWS CodeDeploy) is a deployment service for automating application deployments, not for defining infrastructure. Option D (AWS Elastic Beanstalk) is a platform-as-a-service for deploying web applications, not specifically tailored for serverless architectures.',
