INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_3_43',
  'A developer is preparing a serverless application for deployment. They have defined their AWS Lambda functions, Amazon API Gateway endpoints, and Amazon DynamoDB tables using an AWS SAM template. Which command from the AWS SAM CLI would they typically use to deploy this application to AWS?',
  'mcq',
  '["sam build","sam validate","sam deploy","sam package"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (sam deploy) is the correct command. After building and packaging, `sam deploy` is used to deploy the serverless application defined in the SAM template to AWS CloudFormation. Option A (`sam build`) compiles and packages the application code. Option B (`sam validate`) checks the SAM template for syntax errors. Option D (`sam package`) uploads local artifacts to Amazon S3 and creates a new template with S3 URIs, which is often a precursor to `sam deploy` but `sam deploy` can also handle packaging.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_3_44',
  'A developer is using AWS SAM to define a serverless application. What is the purpose of the `sam build` command?',
  'mcq',
  '["To deploy the serverless application to AWS.","To validate the syntax of the AWS SAM template.","To compile, package, and prepare the application code and dependencies for deployment.","To invoke the Lambda function locally for testing."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (To compile, package, and prepare the application code and dependencies for deployment) is the purpose of the `sam build` command. This command processes the application''s source code, resolves dependencies, and creates a deployable artifact (e.g., a ZIP file for Lambda or a Docker image for container-based functions). Option A (`To deploy the serverless application to AWS`) is handled by `sam deploy`. Option B (`To validate the syntax of the AWS SAM template`) is handled by `sam validate`. Option D (`To invoke the Lambda function locally for testing`) is handled by `sam local invoke`.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_3',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_3_45',
  'A development team is building a serverless application using AWS Lambda and Amazon API Gateway. They need to implement automated integration tests that run as part of their CI/CD pipeline. These tests must validate the end-to-end functionality of the API Gateway endpoints and Lambda functions without deploying to an actual AWS environment, to minimize costs and speed up feedback. Which approach provides the MOST efficient and cost-effective solution for local integration testing?',
  'mcq',
  '["Configure AWS CodeBuild to deploy the serverless application to a dedicated development AWS account and run integration tests against the deployed resources.","Use AWS SAM CLI''s `sam local start-api` command to emulate API Gateway and Lambda locally, then run integration tests against these local endpoints.","Implement a custom Docker Compose setup that mimics API Gateway and Lambda using open-source tools, then execute integration tests against this local environment.","Deploy the serverless application to a staging environment in AWS using AWS CloudFormation and run integration tests there, then tear down the stack."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the most efficient and cost-effective solution for local integration testing. The AWS SAM CLI provides commands like `sam local start-api` that allow developers to run their serverless application locally, emulating Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda. This enables rapid feedback and testing without incurring AWS costs or requiring deployment to a cloud environment.
Option A (incorrect) involves deploying to a dedicated AWS account, which incurs costs and takes longer than local testing, violating the "minimize costs and speed up feedback" constraint. This aligns with anti-pattern [ap-3.2-001].
Option C (incorrect) requires significant custom development and maintenance to mimic AWS services, which is less efficient and more complex than using the purpose-built AWS SAM CLI. It introduces unnecessary operational overhead.
Option D (incorrect) involves deploying to a staging environment in AWS, which incurs costs and deployment time, making it less efficient and cost-effective for rapid, local integration testing compared to using SAM CLI locally. This also aligns with anti-pattern [ap-3.2-001].',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_3',
  'hard'
);

