VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_4_43',
  'A developer needs to manage environment variables for their application within an AWS CodeBuild project. What is the recommended best practice for handling sensitive environment variables, such as API keys, in the `buildspec.yml` file?',
  'mcq',
  '["Store them directly as plaintext environment variables in the `buildspec.yml`.","Store them as plaintext in the CodeBuild project settings.","Reference them from AWS Secrets Manager or AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store SecureString.","Hardcode them directly into the application source code."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Reference them from AWS Secrets Manager or AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store SecureString) is the recommended best practice for handling sensitive environment variables (anti-pattern ap-3.4-001). This ensures that secrets are encrypted at rest and in transit, and access can be controlled via IAM policies. Option A (Store them directly as plaintext environment variables in the `buildspec.yml`) and Option B (Store them as plaintext in the CodeBuild project settings) are insecure as they expose secrets in build logs or the console. Option D (Hardcode them directly into the application source code) is a severe security anti-pattern.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_4',
  'medium'
);

