VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_1_37',
  'A company needs to deploy a web application that runs on Apache Tomcat with Java, requiring automatic scaling and load balancing, but wants to minimize the operational overhead of managing underlying servers. Which AWS service is best suited for this requirement?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EC2 with Auto Scaling Group","AWS Lambda with API Gateway","AWS Elastic Beanstalk","Amazon ECS with Fargate"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS Elastic Beanstalk) is the best choice for this scenario. Elastic Beanstalk is a platform-as-a-service (PaaS) that simplifies the deployment and management of web applications and services. It handles provisioning and managing the underlying infrastructure (EC2 instances, load balancers, Auto Scaling, etc.), significantly reducing operational overhead for common application stacks like Java/Tomcat. Option A (Amazon EC2 with Auto Scaling Group) requires more manual configuration and management of the EC2 instances. Option B (AWS Lambda with API Gateway) is for serverless functions, not traditional web applications running on Tomcat. Option D (Amazon ECS with Fargate) is for containerized applications, which would involve containerizing the Java/Tomcat app and managing ECS, still more overhead than Elastic Beanstalk for this specific use case.',
