  'Option C (Including development dependencies and test files in production deployment artifacts) is an anti-pattern (ap-3.1-001). This practice leads to larger deployment packages, which can increase Lambda cold start times and container pull times, negatively impacting performance and cost. Option A (Using multi-stage Docker builds to minimize image size) and Option B (Excluding development dependencies and test files from production deployment artifacts) are best practices for minimizing artifact size. Option D (Packaging only the necessary application code and runtime dependencies) is also a best practice.',
