  'Option C (Amazon Elastic Container Registry - Amazon ECR) is a fully managed Docker container registry that makes it easy for developers to store, manage, and deploy Docker container images. It integrates seamlessly with Amazon ECS, Amazon E EKS, and AWS Lambda. Option A (Amazon S3) is object storage and while it can store files, it''s not optimized for managing Docker images with versioning and image scanning capabilities. Option B (AWS CodeArtifact) is a fully managed artifact repository service that supports popular package managers like npm, Maven, and NuGet, but not Docker images. Option D (AWS CodeCommit) is a source control service for Git repositories, not a container image registry.',
