  'A developer wants to share common libraries and runtime dependencies across multiple AWS Lambda functions. Order the steps to create and use an AWS Lambda layer.',
  'ordering',
  '["Package the dependencies into a .zip file","Publish the .zip file as a new Lambda layer version","Attach the published layer to the Lambda function","Upload the .zip file to AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'To create and use an AWS Lambda layer, you first package your common libraries and dependencies into a .zip file (Option A). Then, you upload this .zip file to AWS Lambda (Option D). After the upload, you publish it as a new Lambda layer version (Option B), making it available for use. Finally, you attach the published layer to your Lambda function (Option C) so the function can access the shared dependencies.',
