VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_102',
  'A developer needs to configure an AWS Lambda function to send failed asynchronous invocations to a specific Amazon SQS queue for error handling. Order the steps to set up Lambda Destinations for failed invocations.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the Lambda function for asynchronous invocation","Specify the ''OnFailure'' destination for the function","Create an Amazon SQS queue to receive failed events","Define the maximum retry attempts for asynchronous invocations"]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}',
  'To set up Lambda Destinations for failed asynchronous invocations, you first need to create the Amazon SQS queue that will receive the failed events (Option C). Then, ensure your Lambda function is configured for asynchronous invocation (Option A). After that, you specify this SQS queue as the ''OnFailure'' destination for the Lambda function (Option B). Finally, you can define the maximum number of retry attempts for asynchronous invocations before sending to the destination (Option D).',
