INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_105',
  'A developer observes that an AWS Lambda function is performing slowly and wants to optimize its memory configuration to improve performance and potentially reduce cost. Order the steps to tune Lambda memory.',
  'ordering',
  '["Analyze the function''s performance metrics (duration, memory usage)","Adjust the memory setting for the Lambda function","Test the function with different memory configurations","Monitor the function''s cost and performance after changes"]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To tune Lambda memory, you first analyze the function''s current performance metrics, such as duration and memory usage, to identify bottlenecks (Option A). Based on this analysis, you adjust the memory setting for the Lambda function (Option B). Then, you test the function with different memory configurations to find the optimal balance between performance and cost (Option C). Finally, you continuously monitor the function''s cost and performance after implementing changes to ensure the desired outcome (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  30,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_106',
  'A developer is configuring an AWS Lambda function to process messages from an Amazon SQS queue. To prevent poison-pill messages from blocking the queue, a Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) is required. Order the steps to correctly set up an SQS trigger with a DLQ for a Lambda function.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create the primary Amazon SQS queue","Configure the primary SQS queue to use the DLQ","Create the Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) SQS queue","Set up the Lambda function to trigger from the primary SQS queue"]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To correctly set up an SQS trigger with a DLQ for a Lambda function, you first create the primary Amazon SQS queue that will receive initial messages (Option A). Next, you create a separate Dead-Letter Queue (DLQ) SQS queue to hold messages that fail processing (Option C). Then, you configure the primary SQS queue to use the newly created DLQ, specifying retry policies (Option B). Finally, you set up your Lambda function to trigger from the primary SQS queue (Option D), ensuring failed messages are routed to the DLQ.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  31,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_107',
  'A developer is deploying a new AWS Lambda function that has large machine learning libraries as dependencies, exceeding the standard deployment package size limit. Order the approaches to manage these large dependencies efficiently.',
  'ordering',
  '["Remove any unnecessary files or dependencies from the package","Utilize AWS Lambda layers for shared or large libraries","Consider deploying the Lambda function as a container image","Optimize the code to reduce its overall footprint"]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'To manage large Lambda dependencies, first, remove any unnecessary files or dependencies to reduce the package size (Option A). Then, optimize the code itself to reduce its overall footprint (Option D). For shared or large libraries that cannot be easily removed, utilize AWS Lambda layers (Option B) to manage them separately. If dependencies are still too large or complex, consider deploying the Lambda function as a container image (Option C), which supports much larger package sizes (up to 10 GB).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  32,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_108',
  'A team is developing a new feature that requires an AWS Lambda function to access resources within a private Amazon VPC. To enable this secure access, the Lambda function needs to be configured with VPC connectivity. Order the steps to correctly set up the Lambda function for VPC access.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the AWS Lambda function with the selected VPC subnets and security groups.","Create an Amazon VPC with private subnets and a NAT Gateway for outbound internet access.","Ensure the Lambda execution role has the `AWSLambdaVPCAccessExecutionRole` managed policy or equivalent permissions.","Deploy the AWS Lambda function code."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'The first step is to create an Amazon VPC (Option B) with private subnets and a NAT Gateway if outbound internet access is required for the Lambda function. Next, ensure the Lambda execution role has the necessary permissions (Option C), specifically `AWSLambdaVPCAccessExecutionRole`, to manage network interfaces within the VPC. After the role is ready, deploy the AWS Lambda function code (Option D). Finally, configure the AWS Lambda function itself (Option A) by specifying the private subnets and security groups within the VPC, allowing it to access private resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  33,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_109',
  'A developer wants to optimize the cold start performance and execution cost of an AWS Lambda function. They decide to use AWS Lambda Power Tuning to find the optimal memory configuration. Order the steps to effectively use Power Tuning.',
  'ordering',
  '["Deploy the AWS Lambda function to be optimized.","Run the AWS Lambda Power Tuning Step Functions state machine.","Analyze the output from Power Tuning to identify the optimal memory setting for cost and performance.","Update the AWS Lambda function''s memory configuration based on the analysis."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The process starts by deploying the AWS Lambda function (Option A) that needs optimization. Next, the AWS Lambda Power Tuning Step Functions state machine (Option B) is executed, which invokes the Lambda function multiple times with varying memory configurations. After the execution, the output from Power Tuning must be analyzed (Option C) to determine the most cost-effective and performant memory setting. Finally, the AWS Lambda function''s memory configuration is updated (Option D) based on the findings to apply the optimization.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_110',
  'A team is developing a new serverless application that uses AWS Lambda to process data from an Amazon Kinesis Data Stream. To ensure the Lambda function scales efficiently and processes records without issues, they need to configure the event source mapping. Order the steps to set up this integration.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS Lambda function with an execution role that has Kinesis read permissions.","Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Stream.","Configure the Lambda event source mapping to link the Kinesis stream to the Lambda function.","Deploy the AWS Lambda function code that processes Kinesis records."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'The first step is to create an Amazon Kinesis Data Stream (Option B) which will be the source of data. Next, create an AWS Lambda function (Option A) and ensure its execution role has the necessary permissions to read from the Kinesis stream. After the Lambda function is created, deploy its code (Option D) that contains the logic for processing Kinesis records. Finally, configure the Lambda event source mapping (Option C) to establish the connection between the Kinesis stream and the Lambda function, enabling it to automatically process new records.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_111',
  'A developer is building a new AWS Lambda function and wants to manage its concurrency to prevent it from consuming all available account concurrency or overwhelming downstream services. Order the steps to configure reserved concurrency for the Lambda function.',
  'ordering',
  '["Deploy the AWS Lambda function with its initial configuration.","Monitor the AWS Lambda function''s invocation patterns and average concurrency needs.","Set the reserved concurrency limit for the AWS Lambda function.","Adjust the reserved concurrency limit as needed based on observed traffic and performance."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The process begins by deploying the AWS Lambda function (Option A) with its initial configuration. Next, monitor the Lambda function''s invocation patterns (Option B) and average concurrency needs using Amazon CloudWatch to understand its typical usage. Based on this data, set the reserved concurrency limit (Option C) for the Lambda function to ensure it has a dedicated pool of execution environments. Finally, adjust the reserved concurrency limit (Option D) as traffic patterns evolve to maintain optimal performance and cost efficiency.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_112',
  'A developer is building a new feature for an existing application where an AWS Lambda function needs to be invoked directly via HTTP requests. The team wants a simple, secure, and cost-effective way to expose the Lambda function without needing to set up and manage an Amazon API Gateway. The solution should also allow for easy testing and integration.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS Lambda function with the desired business logic.","Invoke the Function URL using an HTTP client (e.g., `curl`, browser, Postman) to test the function.","Configure a Function URL for the AWS Lambda function, specifying the authentication type (e.g., `AWS_IAM` or `NONE`).","Grant appropriate permissions to the Function URL if `AWS_IAM` authentication is chosen."]'::json,
  '{0,2,3,1}',
  'The initial step is to create the AWS Lambda function (Option A) that contains the application''s business logic. Next, configure a Function URL for this Lambda function (Option C), choosing the desired authentication type. If `AWS_IAM` authentication is selected, it''s crucial to grant appropriate permissions (Option D) to the Function URL, typically via an IAM policy, to allow authorized callers to invoke it. Finally, invoke the Function URL (Option B) using an HTTP client to thoroughly test the function''s behavior and ensure it responds as expected.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  37,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_113',
  'A development team wants to process new image uploads to an Amazon S3 bucket using an AWS Lambda function. Order the following steps to configure the S3 bucket to trigger the Lambda function.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS Lambda function with an execution role that has S3 read permissions.","Grant the S3 bucket permission to invoke the Lambda function.","Configure an S3 event notification on the bucket to invoke the Lambda function for specific object events.","Upload an object to the S3 bucket to test the trigger."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'The process of setting up an S3 trigger for a Lambda function begins with the function itself. Option A (Create an AWS Lambda function with an execution role that has S3 read permissions) is the first step, as the Lambda function needs to exist and have the necessary permissions to process S3 events. Option B (Grant the S3 bucket permission to invoke the Lambda function) is crucial for the S3 service to be able to call the Lambda function. Option C (Configure an S3 event notification on the bucket to invoke the Lambda function for specific object events) then establishes the actual trigger mechanism on the S3 bucket. Finally, Option D (Upload an object to the S3 bucket to test the trigger) is the verification step to ensure the setup works as expected.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_114',
  'A developer wants to share common utility code and third-party libraries across multiple AWS Lambda functions without including them in each deployment package. Order the following steps to create and attach a Lambda layer.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a .zip file containing the shared code and dependencies.","Publish the .zip file as a new Lambda layer version.","Configure the Lambda function to use the published layer.","Test the Lambda function to ensure it can access the layer''s content."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Creating and attaching a Lambda layer involves packaging the code, publishing it, and then associating it with the function. Option A (Create a .zip file containing the shared code and dependencies) is the initial step to prepare the layer content. Option B (Publish the .zip file as a new Lambda layer version) makes the layer available for use. Option C (Configure the Lambda function to use the published layer) links the layer to the specific Lambda function. Finally, Option D (Test the Lambda function to ensure it can access the layer''s content) verifies that the layer is correctly integrated and accessible by the function.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  39,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_115',
  'A developer is building an asynchronous AWS Lambda function and wants to ensure that failed invocations are automatically routed to a dead-letter queue for investigation. Order the following steps to configure a Lambda destination for failed asynchronous invocations.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) queue to serve as the dead-letter queue.","Configure the Lambda function''s execution role with permissions to send messages to the SQS queue.","Set the Lambda function''s ''On failure'' destination to the created SQS queue.","Invoke the Lambda function asynchronously with an input that causes a failure to test the destination."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Configuring a Lambda destination for failed asynchronous invocations requires setting up the target, granting permissions, and then linking it to the function. Option A (Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) queue to serve as the dead-letter queue) is the first step, as a destination queue must exist. Option B (Configure the Lambda function''s execution role with permissions to send messages to the SQS queue) ensures the Lambda function has the necessary authorization. Option C (Set the Lambda function''s ''On failure'' destination to the created SQS queue) establishes the routing rule for failed invocations. Finally, Option D (Invoke the Lambda function asynchronously with an input that causes a failure to test the destination) validates the entire setup.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_28_m_28_2_116',
  'A developer is working on an AWS Lambda function and wants to test it locally before deploying to the cloud. Order the following steps to test a Lambda function locally using the AWS Serverless Application Model (SAM) CLI.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define the Lambda function and its API Gateway event in a `template.yaml` file.","Build the serverless application using `sam build`.","Invoke the Lambda function locally using `sam local invoke` or `sam local start-api`.","Install the AWS SAM CLI and Docker on the local development machine."]'::json,
  '{3,0,1,2}',
  'Local testing with SAM CLI requires initial setup, defining the application, building it, and then invoking. Option D (Install the AWS SAM CLI and Docker on the local development machine) is the prerequisite step. Option A (Define the Lambda function and its API Gateway event in a `template.yaml` file) describes the serverless application. Option B (Build the serverless application using `sam build`) prepares the code for local execution. Finally, Option C (Invoke the Lambda function locally using `sam local invoke` or `sam local start-api`) runs the function in a local Docker container, simulating the AWS environment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain28_6',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_28_2',
  'medium'
);

