  'To create a basic Amazon DynamoDB table, you first define the table''s name (Option A). Next, you must specify the primary key, which includes at least a partition key (Option B). Optionally, you can add a sort key to the primary key for more granular querying (Option D). Finally, you set the read/write capacity mode for the table, choosing between On-demand or Provisioned capacity (Option C).',
