  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'To implement Amazon RDS Proxy for efficient database connection management with Lambda, you first need an existing Amazon RDS database instance (Option A). Next, you create an Amazon RDS Proxy (Option B), which acts as an intermediary. Then, you associate this RDS Proxy with your RDS database instance (Option C), linking them together. Finally, you configure your Lambda function to connect to the RDS Proxy endpoint instead of directly to the database (Option D), allowing the proxy to manage the connection pool.',
