  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS CloudFormation) allows you to model and provision AWS resources using templates, serving as the foundation for infrastructure as code. Option B (AWS SAM) extends CloudFormation to simplify the definition of serverless applications. Option C (Amazon EC2) provides virtual servers, not infrastructure as code. Option D (AWS CodeDeploy) is a deployment service, not for defining infrastructure. Option E (AWS CodeCommit) is for source code version control.',
