  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Elastic Beanstalk) is an easy-to-use service for deploying and scaling web applications and services developed with various languages and platforms without managing the underlying infrastructure. Option B (AWS Lambda) allows you to run code without provisioning or managing servers, making it suitable for serverless web application backends. Option C (Amazon EC2) requires server management. Option D (AWS CloudFormation) is for infrastructure as code. Option E (AWS CodeDeploy) is a deployment service, not a compute platform itself.',
