INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_1_101',
  'A developer is setting up a new mobile application that requires user sign-up and sign-in functionality. Order the steps to configure Amazon Cognito User Pools for basic user authentication.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure app clients for the User Pool","Create a new Amazon Cognito User Pool","Integrate the User Pool SDK into the mobile application","Define attributes and password policies"]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'The logical order for setting up an Amazon Cognito User Pool begins with creating the User Pool itself (Option B). Next, you define the user attributes and password policies (Option D) to meet your application''s requirements. After that, you configure app clients (Option A) which are necessary for your application to interact with the User Pool. Finally, you integrate the User Pool SDK into your mobile application (Option C) to enable user sign-up and sign-in.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  1,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_1_102',
  'An AWS Lambda function needs to access an Amazon S3 bucket. Order the steps to grant the Lambda function the necessary permissions using an IAM role.',
  'ordering',
  '["Attach the IAM policy to the IAM role","Create an IAM role with a trust policy for `lambda.amazonaws.com`","Create an IAM policy with `s3:GetObject` permissions for the specific S3 bucket","Assign the IAM role to the Lambda function"]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'To grant a Lambda function permissions, first, create an IAM role (Option B) that the Lambda service can assume, by setting `lambda.amazonaws.com` in its trust policy. Next, create an IAM policy (Option C) that specifies the exact permissions needed, such as `s3:GetObject` for the S3 bucket. Then, attach this newly created IAM policy to the IAM role (Option A). Finally, assign this configured IAM role to your Lambda function (Option D) so it can perform the allowed actions.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_1_103',
  'A developer wants to secure an Amazon API Gateway endpoint using Amazon Cognito User Pools. Order the steps to configure a Cognito User Pool authorizer for the API Gateway.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon Cognito User Pool and an app client","Deploy the API Gateway API","Configure the API Gateway method to use the Cognito User Pool authorizer","Create a new authorizer in API Gateway, selecting ''Cognito'' type"]'::json,
  '{0,3,2,1}',
  'The process begins by ensuring you have an Amazon Cognito User Pool and an app client already set up (Option A), as this is the identity provider. Next, you create a new authorizer in API Gateway (Option D), specifying its type as ''Cognito'' and linking it to your User Pool. After the authorizer is created, you configure the specific API Gateway method (Option C) that needs protection to use this new Cognito User Pool authorizer. The final step is to deploy the API Gateway API (Option B) for the changes to take effect.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_1_104',
  'An application needs temporary AWS credentials to access S3 after a user authenticates with a third-party identity provider. Order the steps to use Amazon Cognito Identity Pools for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure IAM roles for authenticated and unauthenticated users","Create an Amazon Cognito Identity Pool","Integrate the Identity Pool with your application to exchange tokens for AWS credentials","Link the Identity Pool to the third-party identity provider"]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'To vend temporary AWS credentials, first, create an Amazon Cognito Identity Pool (Option B). Then, link this Identity Pool to your chosen third-party identity provider (Option D), such as Google or Facebook. After that, configure the IAM roles (Option A) that the Identity Pool will assume for authenticated and unauthenticated users, defining their permissions. Finally, integrate the Identity Pool SDK into your application (Option C) to exchange the identity provider''s tokens for temporary AWS credentials.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_1_105',
  'A developer needs to assume an IAM role in another AWS account to perform administrative tasks. Order the steps to use AWS STS AssumeRole for cross-account access.',
  'ordering',
  '["Call `sts:AssumeRole` from the source account, passing the target role ARN","Configure an IAM policy in the target account allowing `sts:AssumeRole` for the source account''s principal","Create an IAM role in the target account with the necessary permissions","Receive temporary credentials (Access Key ID, Secret Access Key, Session Token)"]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'The process starts by creating an IAM role in the target account (Option C) that has the specific permissions required for the administrative tasks. Next, you must configure a trust policy on this role in the target account (Option B) to allow the principal from the source account (e.g., an IAM user or role) to assume it. Then, from the source account, make an `sts:AssumeRole` API call (Option A), providing the ARN of the role in the target account. Upon successful assumption, AWS STS returns temporary credentials (Option D) that can be used to access resources in the target account.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_1_106',
  'Order the general steps to create and apply a custom IAM policy for an AWS service.',
  'ordering',
  '["Attach the policy to an IAM user, group, or role","Define the actions (e.g., `s3:PutObject`) and resources (e.g., `arn:aws:s3:::mybucket/*`)","Create a new IAM policy in the IAM console or via API","Specify the effect (Allow or Deny) for the policy statement"]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}',
  'To create and apply a custom IAM policy, first, create a new IAM policy (Option C) in the IAM console or using the AWS CLI/SDK. Within this policy, you then define the specific actions and resources (Option B) that the policy will govern. After that, specify the effect (Option D), either Allow or Deny, for each statement within the policy. Finally, attach this policy to the appropriate IAM user, group, or role (Option A) to grant the defined permissions.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_1_107',
  'A new developer joins the team and needs access to specific AWS resources. Order the steps to grant them access using an existing IAM group.',
  'ordering',
  '["Add the new IAM user to the appropriate IAM group","Create a new IAM user for the developer","Generate access keys for programmatic access (if needed)","Provide the IAM user credentials to the developer"]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'When a new developer joins, the first step is to create a new IAM user for them (Option B). Once the user is created, add this new IAM user to the appropriate IAM group (Option A) that already has the necessary policies attached, inheriting permissions. If programmatic access is required, generate access keys for the IAM user (Option C). Finally, securely provide the IAM user credentials, including the console login URL and any access keys, to the developer (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_1_108',
  'A web application uses Amazon Cognito User Pools for user authentication. Order the steps a user takes to sign in to the application.',
  'ordering',
  '["The application receives the JWT tokens (ID, Access, Refresh)","The user enters their username and password into the application","The application sends the credentials to Amazon Cognito User Pools","Cognito authenticates the user and returns tokens"]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'The user sign-in process begins when the user enters their username and password into the application (Option B). The application then sends these credentials to Amazon Cognito User Pools for authentication (Option C). Cognito processes the credentials, authenticates the user, and if successful, returns JWT tokens (Option D). Finally, the application receives and uses these JWT tokens (Option A) for subsequent authenticated requests to backend services.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_1',
  'easy'
);

