  '{3,2,1,0}',
  'First, an AWS KMS customer managed key needs to be created (Option D) to provide control over the encryption process. Then, the sensitive configuration data is encrypted using this KMS key (Option C). The resulting encrypted configuration data is then stored in a secure location (Option B). Finally, the application is configured to retrieve this encrypted data and use the KMS key to decrypt it at runtime (Option A), ensuring the data is only exposed in plaintext within the application''s secure environment.',
