INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_2_102',
  'A company needs to store highly sensitive customer data in an Amazon S3 bucket and requires that all data be encrypted at rest using a customer-managed key (CMK) from AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS), following an envelope encryption pattern. Order the steps to implement this securely.',
  'ordering',
  '["The application encrypts the data locally using the plaintext data key.","The application requests a plaintext data key and an encrypted copy of the data key from AWS KMS using the CMK.","The application uploads the locally encrypted data and the encrypted data key to Amazon S3.","Create an AWS KMS customer-managed key (CMK) and grant the application''s IAM role permissions to use it for `kms:GenerateDataKey` and `kms:Decrypt`."]'::json,
  '{3,1,0,2}',
  'To implement envelope encryption for S3 data using a KMS CMK, first create the AWS KMS CMK (Option D) and grant the application''s IAM role the necessary permissions. Next, the application requests a plaintext data key and its encrypted counterpart from AWS KMS (Option B). Then, the application uses the plaintext data key to encrypt the sensitive data locally (Option A). Finally, the application uploads both the locally encrypted data and the encrypted data key to Amazon S3 (Option C), ensuring the plaintext data key is never stored with the data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  44,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_2_103',
  'A developer needs to configure automatic rotation for a database credential stored in AWS Secrets Manager, ensuring that the application can retrieve the updated secret seamlessly. Order the steps to set up this automated rotation.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the rotation schedule and specify the Lambda rotation function in AWS Secrets Manager for the secret.","Create an AWS Secrets Manager secret to store the database credentials.","Develop an AWS Lambda function that contains the logic to rotate the database credential.","Grant the Lambda rotation function the necessary permissions to access Secrets Manager and the database."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'To set up automatic rotation for a database credential in AWS Secrets Manager, first create the AWS Secrets Manager secret (Option B) to store the initial database credentials. Next, develop an AWS Lambda function (Option C) that implements the specific logic for rotating the credentials in the database and updating the secret. Then, grant this Lambda rotation function (Option D) the necessary IAM permissions to interact with Secrets Manager and the database. Finally, configure the rotation schedule for the secret in AWS Secrets Manager (Option A), specifying the Lambda function to be used for rotation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  45,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_2_104',
  'A web application hosted on Amazon EC2 instances needs to retrieve a non-rotating API key securely from AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as a SecureString. Order the steps to store and retrieve this secret.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the Amazon EC2 instance''s IAM role with permissions to call `ssm:GetParameters` or `ssm:GetParameter` for the specific SecureString parameter.","The application code on the EC2 instance uses the AWS SDK to retrieve the SecureString parameter, specifying `WithDecryption`.","Create a SecureString parameter in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store, storing the API key.","Ensure the IAM role has permissions to use the AWS KMS key associated with the SecureString for decryption."]'::json,
  '{2,0,3,1}',
  'To securely store and retrieve a non-rotating API key as a SecureString from AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store, first create the SecureString parameter (Option C) in Parameter Store. Next, configure the Amazon EC2 instance''s IAM role (Option A) with permissions to retrieve this specific parameter. Then, ensure this IAM role also has permissions (Option D) to use the AWS KMS key that encrypted the SecureString for decryption. Finally, the application code on the EC2 instance (Option B) uses the AWS SDK to retrieve the parameter, explicitly requesting decryption.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  46,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_2_105',
  'A developer needs to ensure that all objects uploaded to an existing Amazon S3 bucket are automatically encrypted at rest using server-side encryption with AWS KMS (SSE-KMS). Order the steps to configure this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the S3 bucket''s default encryption settings to use SSE-KMS with the specified KMS key.","Create an AWS KMS customer-managed key (CMK) or choose an existing one.","Grant the IAM principal (user or role) uploading objects to the S3 bucket permissions to use the specified KMS key for encryption.","Upload objects to the S3 bucket; they will now be automatically encrypted with SSE-KMS."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To enforce SSE-KMS for an S3 bucket, first create or select an AWS KMS customer-managed key (CMK) (Option B). Next, configure the S3 bucket''s default encryption settings (Option A) to use SSE-KMS with this specific KMS key. Then, ensure that the IAM principal (Option C) responsible for uploading objects has the necessary permissions to use the specified KMS key for encryption. Finally, when objects are uploaded to the S3 bucket (Option D), they will automatically be encrypted using SSE-KMS.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  47,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_2_106',
  'A company requires all data in transit to its web application, fronted by an Application Load Balancer (ALB), to be encrypted using HTTPS. Order the steps to configure the ALB for secure TLS/SSL termination.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the Application Load Balancer (ALB) listener to listen on HTTPS (port 443) and associate the SSL/TLS certificate.","Create an SSL/TLS certificate using AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) or import an existing one.","Update DNS records to point the domain name to the ALB''s DNS name.","Configure the ALB listener to redirect HTTP (port 80) traffic to HTTPS (port 443)."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'To enforce HTTPS for an ALB, first create or import an SSL/TLS certificate using AWS Certificate Manager (Option B). Next, configure the Application Load Balancer (ALB) listener (Option A) to listen on HTTPS (port 443) and associate this certificate. Then, configure an additional ALB listener (Option D) on HTTP (port 80) to redirect all incoming HTTP traffic to the HTTPS listener. Finally, update the DNS records (Option C) for the application''s domain to point to the ALB''s DNS name, ensuring all traffic goes through the ALB and is encrypted.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_2_107',
  'A developer needs to create a new AWS KMS customer managed key (CMK) and then grant a specific IAM role permission to use this CMK for encryption and decryption operations. Order the steps to achieve this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a new AWS KMS customer managed key (CMK) with a custom key policy.","Attach an IAM policy to the specific IAM role, granting `kms:Encrypt` and `kms:Decrypt` permissions on the CMK''s ARN.","Define the key policy for the CMK, ensuring it allows the IAM role to perform key usage operations.","Verify the IAM role can successfully encrypt and decrypt data using the CMK."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To create a KMS CMK and grant an IAM role access, first create a new AWS KMS CMK (Option A). Next, define the key policy for this CMK (Option C), explicitly allowing the target IAM role to perform key usage operations. Then, attach an IAM policy to the specific IAM role (Option B), granting it `kms:Encrypt` and `kms:Decrypt` permissions on the CMK''s ARN. Finally, verify that the IAM role can successfully use the CMK (Option D) for encryption and decryption.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_2_108',
  'A company wants to host a static website on Amazon S3 and serve it securely over HTTPS using a custom domain name, with content delivery optimized by Amazon CloudFront. Order the steps to configure this setup.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the Amazon S3 bucket for static website hosting and upload the website content.","Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution, pointing its origin to the S3 bucket''s website endpoint and associating the ACM certificate.","Create an SSL/TLS certificate for the custom domain name in AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) in the US East (N. Virginia) region.","Update the DNS records for the custom domain to point to the CloudFront distribution''s domain name."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To host a secure static website on S3 with CloudFront, first configure the Amazon S3 bucket (Option A) for static website hosting and upload the content. Next, create an SSL/TLS certificate for the custom domain in AWS Certificate Manager (Option C) in `us-east-1`. Then, create an Amazon CloudFront distribution (Option B), using the S3 website endpoint as the origin and associating the ACM certificate. Finally, update the DNS records (Option D) for the custom domain to point to the CloudFront distribution''s domain name.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain29_6',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_29_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_29_m_29_2_109',
  'A developer needs to implement client-side encryption for objects uploaded to Amazon S3 using a customer-provided encryption key (SSE-C). Order the steps for the application to encrypt and upload an object.',
  'ordering',
  '["The application generates a unique encryption key for the object.","The application sends the encrypted object to Amazon S3 along with the encryption key and its MD5 hash in the request headers.","The application encrypts the object data locally using the generated encryption key.","The application calculates the MD5 hash of the encryption key."]'::json,
  '{0,2,3,1}',
  'For client-side encryption with SSE-C, the application first generates a unique encryption key (Option A) for the specific object. Next, it encrypts the object data locally (Option C) using this generated key. Then, the application calculates the MD5 hash of the encryption key (Option D). Finally, the application sends the encrypted object to Amazon S3 (Option B) along with the encryption key and its MD5 hash in the required HTTP headers (`x-amz-server-side-encryption-customer-key` and `x-amz-server-side-encryption-customer-key-MD5`).',
