  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'To store a third-party API key, first, store the API key as an ''Other type of secret'' in AWS Secrets Manager (Option B), as it doesn''t fit predefined types like database credentials. Next, configure an IAM policy (Option C) that grants the `secretsmanager:GetSecretValue` permission for that specific secret to your application''s IAM role. Then, retrieve the API key in your application code (Option A) using the AWS SDK. Since automatic rotation is not supported, you will need to manually update the secret in Secrets Manager (Option D) whenever the third-party API key changes.',
