  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'To access a database password from Secrets Manager in a Lambda function, first create an AWS Secrets Manager secret (Option B) to store the password. Next, configure the Lambda function''s execution role (Option C) with an IAM policy that grants `secretsmanager:GetSecretValue` permission, scoped to the specific secret''s ARN. Then, deploy the AWS Lambda function (Option D), ensuring the password is not hardcoded or exposed. Finally, the Lambda function''s code (Option A) uses the AWS SDK to call `secretsmanager.getSecretValue` to retrieve the password at runtime.',
