INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_3_81',
  'A developer is setting up a new serverless application using AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM). Order the essential AWS SAM CLI commands to initialize, build, and deploy the application.',
  'ordering',
  '["Run `sam deploy --guided` to deploy the application","Run `sam build` to compile the application code and dependencies","Run `sam init` to create a new SAM project","Run `sam validate` to check the SAM template for errors"]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}',
  'The correct sequence for deploying a serverless application with AWS SAM CLI begins with initializing the project. Option C (`sam init`) creates the basic project structure. Next, Option B (`sam build`) compiles the application code and dependencies, preparing them for deployment. After building, it''s good practice to validate the template with Option D (`sam validate`) to catch any syntax or logical errors before deployment. Finally, Option A (`sam deploy --guided`) deploys the application to AWS CloudFormation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  1,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_3_82',
  'A development team needs to deploy infrastructure as code using AWS CloudFormation. Order the steps to define and deploy a new CloudFormation stack.',
  'ordering',
  '["Upload the CloudFormation template to an Amazon S3 bucket (if not using inline template)","Define the infrastructure in a CloudFormation template (YAML or JSON)","Create the CloudFormation stack using the AWS Management Console or AWS CLI","Review the stack events and resources after deployment"]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'The process of deploying a CloudFormation stack starts with defining the infrastructure. Option B involves writing the CloudFormation template in YAML or JSON. Next, Option A is to upload this template to an Amazon S3 bucket, which is a common practice for larger templates or when using the CLI/SDK. Then, Option C is to initiate the stack creation process. Finally, Option D involves monitoring the stack creation events and verifying the deployed resources to ensure success.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_3_83',
  'To efficiently test an AWS Lambda function locally using the AWS SAM CLI, a developer needs to follow a specific sequence of actions. Order these actions.',
  'ordering',
  '["Prepare a test event payload in a JSON file","Run `sam local invoke MyFunction -e event.json`","Navigate to the root directory of the SAM project","Execute `sam build` to prepare the function for local invocation"]'::json,
  '{2,3,0,1}',
  'To test a Lambda function locally with SAM CLI, the first step is to ensure you are in the correct context. Option C, navigating to the SAM project''s root directory, is essential. Then, Option D (`sam build`) is required to compile the application and prepare it for local execution. After the build, Option A involves creating a JSON file with the event payload that the Lambda function will process. Finally, Option B (`sam local invoke`) is used to execute the function locally with the specified event.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_3_84',
  'When structuring an AWS Serverless Application Model (SAM) template, there''s a typical order for the top-level sections. Order these common SAM template sections.',
  'ordering',
  '["Resources section, defining serverless functions, APIs, and databases","AWSTemplateFormatVersion, specifying the template format version","Parameters section, for input values to customize the template","Globals section, for common properties across serverless resources"]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'A well-structured AWS SAM template typically starts with metadata. Option B, `AWSTemplateFormatVersion`, is the very first required section. Following this, Option C, the `Parameters` section, allows for input values to customize the template. Option D, the `Globals` section, defines common properties that apply to multiple serverless resources. Finally, Option A, the `Resources` section, is where the actual serverless functions, APIs, and other AWS resources are defined.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_3',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_30_m_30_3_85',
  'A developer needs to update an existing AWS Lambda function managed by an AWS SAM template. Order the steps to modify and redeploy the function.',
  'ordering',
  '["Run `sam deploy --guided` to apply the changes to AWS","Modify the Lambda function code or the SAM template configuration","Test the updated function locally using `sam local invoke`","Execute `sam build` to recompile the application artifacts"]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'The process of updating a Lambda function managed by SAM starts with the actual changes. Option B is to modify the function code or the SAM template. After making changes, Option C, testing locally with `sam local invoke`, is crucial for verifying functionality before deployment. Then, Option D (`sam build`) recompiles the updated application artifacts. Finally, Option A (`sam deploy --guided`) pushes these changes to the AWS environment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain30_6',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_30_3',
