  'A developer needs to manage sensitive environment variables in an AWS CodeBuild project securely. Order the steps to achieve this using AWS Secrets Manager or Parameter Store SecureString.',
  'ordering',
  '["Reference the environment variable in the `buildspec.yml` file","Configure the CodeBuild project''s service role to grant access to the secret","Store the sensitive value as a SecureString in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store or a secret in AWS Secrets Manager","Retrieve the secret value during the CodeBuild execution"]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}',
  'Securely managing secrets in CodeBuild starts with storing the secret in a dedicated service. Option C is to store the sensitive value in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as a SecureString or in AWS Secrets Manager. Next, Option B involves configuring the CodeBuild project''s service role to ensure it has the necessary permissions to access this secret. Then, Option A is to reference this secure environment variable in the `buildspec.yml` file. Finally, Option D is when CodeBuild automatically retrieves the secret value during the build execution, making it available to your build commands.',
