  '{1,0,3,2}',
  'A typical AWS CodePipeline starts with the Source stage (Option B), which retrieves the application code from a version control repository like AWS CodeCommit. Next is the Build stage (Option A), where the code is compiled, dependencies are installed, and unit tests are run. Following this is the Test stage (Option D), dedicated to running integration or acceptance tests against the built artifacts. Finally, the Deploy stage (Option C) releases the application to its target environments, such as Amazon EC2, AWS Lambda, or Amazon ECS.',
