  'A typical CodeDeploy `AppSpec` file starts with the `version` section (Option C) to specify the file format version. Next is the `files` section (Option B), which defines which application files from the source revision should be copied to the target instances. Then, the `permissions` section (Option D) is used to set file and directory permissions for the copied files. Finally, the `hooks` section (Option A) specifies scripts to run at different stages of the deployment lifecycle, such as `BeforeInstall` or `ApplicationStart`.',
